- **F03-5** `crates/c3/src/work/record.rs:137`, `crates/c3/src/work/record.rs:187`, `crates/c3/src/work/record.rs:211` - Q3/F91-2 remedy: make admission fail closed on uninspectable records. read_record (record.rs:137) maps every fs::read error to Ok(None), run_dirs (record.rs:187) returns [] on read_dir failure and flattens entry errors, and live_run/other_live_run (record.rs:211/223) discard read errors via .ok(), so a live worker whose run.json is unreadable is invisible to the one-live-worker guard. Verify: New tests read_record_distinguishes_notfound_from_unreadable (missing dir yields Ok(None); a run.json made unreadable, e.g. replaced by a directory, yields Err) and admission_refuses_when_candidate_uninspectable (other_live_run/live_run return Err and claim_for_spawn refuses before writing running). Plus the RC1 denied-read fixture with a live blocking worker: second same-task command refuses with no launch marker. Remedy: Distinguish error kinds: only ErrorKind::NotFound maps to Ok(None); all other read errors, plus directory enumeration and entry errors, propagate as Err. Change run_dirs, live_run and other_live_run to return Result and make both admission callers (run() start path and claim_for_spawn) refuse admission on Err. Invariant: admission proceeds only when every candidate record was inspected or confirmed absent; uninspectable state is a refusal, never an empty list. Parse errors already return Err and keep doing so.

### Unproven scenarios

- No tests or builds were run (read-only consultation); all Q3 remedies are code-inspected designs, not implemented or executed.
- Whether pack-only solvers produce implementable proposals without repo access is untested; the pilot in finding #1 is the proposed measurement.
- Router internals (crates/c3/src/router/) and panel roles (crates/c3/src/panel/roles.rs) were not read; Q2/Q4 assume the brief's description of them.
