## Framing first

The brief's own pass-2 evidence undercuts the premise: F91-1 and F91-3 are "the fix closed the simple case, this is the remaining case" — a **verification gap**, not a design gap. Astra's one-sentence remedies were adequate directions; what was missing is that nobody executed Astra's own RC1–RC3 fixtures between passes. Options the brief does not list:

- **O1: test-first worker briefs.** The worker must write a failing test that drives the finding's trigger *before* the fix, and the next acceptance pass runs it. Cost: zero extra consultations.
- **O2: the finder's `remedy` becomes acceptance criteria.** The finder already wrote RC1–RC3; the coordinator can turn those into the worker's definition of done instead of paying three solvers.
- **O3: remedy panel as proposed.** Pays ~3 consultations per blocker for design diversity.

To choose I would need: the per-release window budget vs. deadline, and whether the roster workers can run `cargo test` in-tree (O1/O2 need it; O3 does not). My recommendation: O1+O2 by default, O3 only when two consecutive passes fail the *same* finding — i.e., escalate to solvers on demonstrated design failure, not on every blocker.

## Q1. Roles

Sound, with the verifier being **a shipped test, then the finder**. The solver must ship the test that drives the trigger; the finder verifies on the next pass against criteria it stated when raising the finding. Failure modes: (a) solver ignorant of the codebase — mitigated by the pack of located code plus nearest existing tests; (b) finder rejecting every foreign fix — mitigated by requiring the finder to state acceptance criteria up front, so a rejection must cite a failed criterion or a *new* trigger (a new trigger is a new finding, credited as such, not a veto); (c) cost — gate remedy panels on blockers only, and batch same-file findings into one remedy consultation.

## Q2. Minimal record and workflow

`findings[].proposals[]` = `{proposer, approach, locations, patch_sketch, test, risks, confidence, status: proposed|adopted|rejected, reason}` — one JSON object per proposal inside the existing `findings.json`; nothing else new. Purpose `remedy`, preset effort high, `--exclude-vendor <finder lab>`, pack = the finding record + located files + the tests that exist. The coordinator records adoption by setting `status`+`reason`. Never automate: the adoption choice, the decision to spend the window (the `--remedy` line is offered, not run), and the `verified` flip (finder-only).

## Q3. Concrete remedies

**F91-1 (blocker, stale admission).** Change `claim_for_spawn` (`work/mod.rs:747`) to take `expected_attempt` instead of `attempt`; under the lock it already rereads the record — extend that reread to refuse when the record is terminal (`done`, `quota` with `exhausted`), and when `rec.attempt + 1 != expected_attempt`; set `rec.attempt = rec.attempt + 1` computed from the locked record. Invariant: the locked record alone authorizes the attempt number and the claim. Test `resume_after_terminal_refused`: barrier before the second claim, first attempt reaches `done` (and separately `quota` with `exhausted:true`); the delayed resume must refuse with no launch marker and an unchanged `run.json`.

**F91-2 (blocker, unreadable = absent).** In `record.rs`, make `read_record` return `Ok(None)` only on `ErrorKind::NotFound` and `Err` on every other I/O error; make `run_dirs` return `Result` propagating enumeration and entry errors; make `live_run`/`other_live_run` return `Result<Option<String>>`; `claim_for_spawn` refuses on any `Err`. Invariant: admission requires *positive* confirmation no other run is live. Test `admission_refuses_on_unreadable_record`: live worker plus injected `PermissionDenied` on its `run.json`; second start must refuse pre-launch.

**F91-3 (major, destructive artifact reads).** In `refresh_artifacts` (`mod.rs:858`), read `events.jsonl` with error propagation when the file exists; on `Err` the caller finishes `artifact_error` and keeps the previous `report.md`. In `resume_once`, read both temp attempt files *before* `append_resume`, propagate failures through `finish_artifact_error`, and delete the temp files only after the append has durably succeeded. Invariant: bytes are deleted only after their contents are incorporated. Test `artifact_read_failure_preserves_bytes`: injected read failures on attempt and aggregate streams; expect nonzero exit, `artifact_error`, retained bytes, old report intact.

**F91-4 (major, weak terminal evidence).** Claude: in the `has_result` path require `is_error == Some(false)` and a non-empty `result` string, else `Terminal::None`. Codex (`engines.rs:501-514`): only `turn.completed` sets `saw_completed`; keep the `agent_message` parse solely for report extraction in `summarize`. Fix the codified wrong expectation at `engines.rs:651-652`. Test `terminal_requires_affirmative_success`: both streams from the finding with exit 0 classify `died` through `classify_attempt`.

## Q4. Scoring

Credit the solver only on `adopted` **and** `verified` (adoption alone is coordinator taste; verification is ground truth). Credit the finder for the finding itself, not for the fix — otherwise finder and solver incentives couple. Anti-gaming: a blocker later `rejected` counts against the finder's precision; a solver whose verified fix resurfaces as "the remaining case" in the next pass loses the solver credit retroactively. This makes "good solver" mean "fixes stay closed", which is exactly what passes 1–2 lacked.

## Requested checks

- **RC1:** Repository root; workspace-write; `cargo test -p c3 work` after implementing findings #3–#6; require the four new tests to fail before the fix and pass after. Budget: 15 minutes.
- **RC2:** Repository root; read-only; confirm a `c3 work` worker wave can execute `cargo test` in-tree (check the worker's sandbox/permissions in `docs/work-mode.md` against a real wave log); settles whether option O1 (test-first briefs) is viable without the remedy panel. Budget: 5 minutes.

### Findings

- **F07-1** [note] (no location) - Default to test-first worker briefs with the finder's requested checks as acceptance criteria (options O1+O2); escalate to a remedy panel (O3) only when the same finding survives two fix passes, because pass-2 evidence shows a verification gap, not a design gap. Trigger: Any acceptance HOLD whose findings are 'the fix closed the simple case' of an earlier blocker. Evidence: read-code: F91-1 and F91-3 supersede F89-2/F89-3 as remaining cases; Astra supplied executable checks RC1-RC3 that were never run between passes.; inferred: 280s and 9-16% window per pass; remedy panels triple consultation cost per blocker. Verify: Run RC2 to confirm workers can execute tests in-tree; if yes, pilot O1 on the next blocker and compare pass count to closure against the 0.2.3 loop. Remedy: Brief the worker with the finding's trigger plus a mandatory failing test first; the finder verifies the test on the next pass. Reserve the solver panel for repeat failures.
- **F07-2** [note] (no location) - The minimal proposals record is {proposer, approach, locations, patch_sketch, test, risks, confidence, status, reason} stored in findings.json under the finding id; adoption, rejection reasons, the decision to spend the window, and the verified flip must stay manual. Trigger: Designing the remedy purpose and its ledger footprint. Evidence: read-code: Brief lists existing findings[].remedy, prior_findings, panel roles, routing, packs; coordinator's sketch already stores proposals under the finding id. Verify: Schema-review the proposed record against crates/c3/src/consult/ ingestion and `c3 findings` status transitions in a follow-up consult. Remedy: Add findings[].proposals[] as plain JSON in the existing findings store; add purpose `remedy` with vendor exclusion and a pack of finding record + located code + existing tests. Never auto-adopt or auto-verify.
- **F07-3** [blocker] `crates/c3/src/work/mod.rs:747` - Proposed remedy for F91-1: claim_for_spawn must validate status, exhaustion and expected attempt generation from the record it rereads under the admission lock, and compute the next attempt from that locked record. Trigger: A delayed resume passes pre-lock checks, then claims a record that became done or quota-exhausted, reusing a stale attempt number. Evidence: read-code: The locked reread checks only other live runs and a different live owner, then unconditionally sets running with the caller-supplied attempt. Verify: New test resume_after_terminal_refused: barrier before the second claim; first attempt reaches done, separately quota-exhausted; the delayed resume refuses with no child-launch marker and an unchanged run.json. Remedy: Change claim_for_spawn to take expected_attempt; under the lock refuse when the reread record is terminal, quota.exhausted, or rec.attempt + 1 != expected_attempt; set rec.attempt = rec.attempt + 1 from the locked record.
- **F07-4** [blocker] `crates/c3/src/work/record.rs:137`, `crates/c3/src/work/record.rs:187`, `crates/c3/src/work/record.rs:211`, `crates/c3/src/work/record.rs:223` - Proposed remedy for F91-2: only a confirmed NotFound may count as an absent record; every other inspection error must propagate to admission, which refuses. Trigger: A live worker's run.json cannot be read (permissions) or its directory cannot be enumerated; a second start or resume skips the live run. Evidence: read-code: read_record maps every fs::read error to Ok(None); run_dirs returns empty on enumeration failure and flattens entry errors; live_run and other_live_run discard record errors. Verify: New test admission_refuses_on_unreadable_record: live worker plus injected PermissionDenied on its run.json; a second same-task start must refuse before any launch marker. Remedy: Match ErrorKind::NotFound to Ok(None) in read_record and Err on all other I/O errors; make run_dirs, live_run and other_live_run return Result; claim_for_spawn refuses on any Err.
- **F07-5** [major] `crates/c3/src/work/mod.rs:858`, `crates/c3/src/work/mod.rs:1175` - Proposed remedy for F91-3: event-file read errors become artifact errors; temporary attempt files survive until their contents are durably incorporated; an unreadable aggregate stream never replaces a valid report. Trigger: Reading an attempt's temp events file fails while removal still succeeds, or a transient read failure on events.jsonl during refresh_artifacts follows a successfully classified attempt. Evidence: read-code: refresh_artifacts uses read_to_string(...).unwrap_or_default() for events.jsonl and writes the resulting report without surfacing a read error. Verify: New test artifact_read_failure_preserves_bytes: injected read failures on the attempt and aggregate event files; expect nonzero exit, artifact_error, retained source bytes, and the prior report.md intact. Remedy: Propagate events.jsonl read errors from refresh_artifacts when the file exists; read attempt temp files before append, finish artifact_error on failure, delete temp files only after a durably successful append.
- **F07-6** [major] `crates/c3/src/work/engines.rs:476`, `crates/c3/src/work/engines.rs:503`, `crates/c3/src/work/engines.rs:651` - Proposed remedy for F91-4: Claude success requires an explicitly valid result (is_error present and false, non-empty result text); Codex success requires turn.completed alone, with agent_message used only for report extraction; the unit test at engines.rs:651 codifies the bug and must be inverted. Trigger: An exit-zero launcher emits {"type":"result"} with no is_error (Claude) or only an agent_message item.completed (Codex), then ends without a successful terminal. Evidence: read-code: Claude maps has_result with is_error false (absent counts) to Success; Codex sets saw_completed for an agent_message item.completed as well as turn.completed.; read-code: terminal_outcome_reads_the_stream asserts Success for a Codex agent_message-only stream. Verify: New test terminal_requires_affirmative_success driving both stated streams with exit code 0 through classify_attempt; require died in both cases, never done. Remedy: Tighten the Claude branch to require is_error == Some(false) and a non-empty result; restrict the Codex saw_completed flag to turn.completed and keep agent_message parsing in summarize only; update the existing test expectation.
- **F07-7** [note] (no location) - Scoring: credit the solver only on adopted AND verified, credit the finder only for the finding, penalize a rejected blocker against finder precision, and revoke solver credit when a verified fix resurfaces as a remaining case in the next pass. Trigger: Feeding remedy outcomes into the router as a second 'solver' dimension without letting finders game it with easy blockers. Evidence: inferred: Adoption alone is coordinator taste; the 0.2.3 loop shows fixes that pass adoption but fail the next review, so verification is the only ground truth available. Verify: Simulate the pass-1/pass-2 0.2.3 history under the proposed credit rules and confirm the wave-10a worker fixes would not have earned lasting solver credit. Remedy: Store adoption and verification as separate router signals; solver score = verified/(adopted); finder precision = confirmed/(raised); resurface of the same case decrements the prior solver credit.

