- **RC1:** Repository root; workspace-write; add and run `resume_claim_rejects_stale_snapshot` using deterministic barriers and launch markers. Finding #4 is confirmed if stale admission launches; closure requires all rejection cases and the alarm control. Budget: 30 minutes.
- **RC2:** Repository root; workspace-write; add and run `admission_fails_closed_on_inspection_error` with injected filesystem failures. Finding #5 is confirmed if uncertainty permits launch; closure requires all refusal cases and controls. Budget: 30 minutes.

### Findings

- **F12-1** [note] `.collab/consilium-2026-10-22/handoffs/01-claude-remedy-proposals.md` - Pilot an invariant-driven workflow with one solver and conditional independent review; the reported acceptance loop does not establish that separating finder and solver identities will reduce recurrence. Trigger: Repeated acceptance failures lead to a proposal for multiple remedy consultations per blocker. Evidence: read-code: The brief describes two acceptance passes, implementation between them, and substantial consultation and worker costs; it provides no comparison of alternative workflows.; inferred: The observed gaps concern transition preconditions and incomplete error propagation, both of which require explicit invariant coverage regardless of solver identity. Verify: Compare a bounded set of similar repairs using one solver plus explicit invariant tests against independent alternatives, recording total closure time, reviewer cost and reopened defects. Remedy: Start with a reproducer and acceptance criteria, then assign one solver per related invariant cluster; allow the finder to contribute a design without making it authoritative. The finder checks the original trigger, the coordinator assesses the patch and regressions, and a third reviewer resolves criterion disputes or substantial residual risk. Require rejection to identify a counterexample or violated criterion, and select panel size using repository familiarity, context completeness, recurrence causes and measured closure cost.
- **F12-2** [note] `crates/c3-core/src/findings.rs:113`, `crates/c3-core/src/findings.rs:158` - Proposal provenance and selection history must remain separate from finding status and verification evidence. Trigger: A coordinator adopts, combines, revises or declines competing proposals, potentially against different code revisions. Evidence: read-code: Finding stores source, status history and reviewer checks; unknown members survive rewrites through extra, and set_status binds transitions to history events.; read-code: The design makes files authoritative and keeps reviewer execution read-only. Verify: Round-trip a finding containing two proposals and a merged decision through existing finding operations; require preserved provenance, append-only decision history and unchanged finding status until an explicit supported transition. Remedy: Record proposal ID, finding IDs, consult ID, reviewer identity, code/finding/pack digests, approach, locations, patch sketch, invariant, test specification, assumptions and risks, with immutable reply references. Append decisions recording actor, timestamp, selected IDs and rationale; give merged designs a new ID with parent links and attach the eventual implementation revision. Distinguish not_selected from technically rejected, and keep adoption independent of implemented or verified finding status.
- **F12-3** [note] `.collab/consilium-2026-10-22/handoffs/01-claude-remedy-proposals.md`, `docs/DESIGN.md:135` - A solver needs invariant-relevant context and explicit eligibility rules; cited code alone and blanket vendor exclusion are insufficient selection criteria. Trigger: A repository-unfamiliar reviewer receives a generated pack, or excluding the finder's vendor removes the available qualified solver. Evidence: read-code: The sketch proposes packs from finding locations and existing tests, exclusion of the finder's vendor, and automatic preparation of a remedy command.; read-code: The alarm has an owner-preserving waiting state, and a nominal record reader performs recovery writes; these affect a correct admission remedy beyond the original locked claim. Verify: Review a generated F91-1 pack against an explicit dependency checklist and inspect its proposed roster when an exclusion leaves insufficient eligible solvers. Remedy: Pilot an existing solver role before adding a remedy purpose, supplying callers, writers, state definitions, liveness/locking dependencies, error paths, tests and disclosed omissions in the pack. Prefer qualified independent laboratories while preserving explicit coordinator-provider exclusions and never silently relaxing constraints. Automate preparation and validation, but leave consultation spending, proposal selection/merging, worker execution and verification decisions with the coordinator.
