## Framing

The panel treats "remedy is a direction" as the root cause; pass 2 suggests another. Every F91 finding supersedes a pass-1 finding whose fix "closed the simple case": the finder never stated what evidence closes the bug, so the worker fixed the named case, not the invariant. Unlisted options:

1. **Criteria-first, no new consultations** — the finder writes `acceptance[]` (test name + what it drives, or the exact refusal) before any fix; the next pass, already paid for, verifies. Trial this for one loop before building a purpose.
2. **Escalation, not default** — three seats per blocker ≈ 3 × 9–16 % of the window plus a worker wave; two blockers can exceed half the window. Convene the panel only when a finding supersedes a prior one (repeat failure) or criteria conflict; otherwise one solver.

To choose: whether pass-2 misses were cases an independent solver would have listed or only explicit criteria pin down; the supersedes rate across `.collab`; which roster members read the repo versus need a pack.

## Q1 — roles

Sound, two amendments. Verifier: the solver's shipped test plus the finder's pre-committed acceptance criteria, adjudicated by the finder on its next pass — not a third member (a window share for no information the finder's pass lacks). Failure modes: a solver ignorant of the codebase — require exact function names and a compiling test, and prefer repo-reading engines (claude/codex) as solvers; a pack-fed solver cannot see that a `record.rs` signature change must also update the caller in `run()` (mod.rs:904). A finder that rejects foreign fixes — criteria are committed before proposals are visible, and the finder judges only against them. Cost of three consultations — escalation above.

## Q2 — minimal record

Add `findings[].acceptance[]` (finder, before proposals are visible) and `findings[].proposals[]` {proposer, approach, locations, patch_sketch, test{name, drives}, risks, confidence}; lifecycle proposed → adopted|rejected(reason) → verified|failed on the finder's pass. Purpose `remedy`, seats via roles.rs, brief generated from the finding record plus a pack of the located functions, their callers, and the existing tests. Not automated: the adoption choice, the finder's criteria, worker execution, and `verified` (test-green alone is not finder confirmation); the router must not read `adopted` as skill.

## Q3 — proposals (I am not the finder)

- **F91-1:** derive everything under the lock. `claim_for_spawn` (mod.rs:747) refuses terminal/exhausted records and computes `n` itself from the locked reread — `resume_once` computes `n` pre-lock at mod.rs:1142, and the `is_pending` guard at mod.rs:755 waves a `done` record through. Test `resume_refuses_when_record_became_terminal_between_read_and_claim`: barrier before the second claim; the first resume reaches done/exhausted; the second must refuse, no second launch marker.
- **F91-2:** absence must be proven. `read_record` (record.rs:137) returns Ok(None) only on NotFound, Err otherwise; `run_dirs` (187) propagates enumeration/entry errors; `live_run`/`other_live_run` (211/223) become Results and admission refuses on any uninspectable record. Test `admission_refuses_when_live_record_unreadable`: live worker, denied read on its run.json, second start refuses.
- **F91-3:** propagate the reads. `refresh_artifacts` (mod.rs:858) and `resume_once` (1175–1176) replace `unwrap_or_default` with errors ending in `artifact_error`; keep tmp attempt files until read and durably appended — an unread tmp today "appends" empty at 1188, then is deleted at 1192.
- **F91-4:** affirmative terminals only. The Claude arm (engines.rs:478) requires explicit `is_error:false` — absent means Terminal::None; Codex drops the agent_message branch (engines.rs:504–512), success = `turn.completed` only, message extraction separate. Test `exit_zero_without_affirmative_terminal_is_not_done`; flip the unit at engines.rs:642 asserting the opposite today.

## Q4 — scoring

Credit the solver only on `verified` (adopted-but-failed pays nothing — the worker may have implemented badly). Finder and solver are separate, non-zero-sum dimensions. Anti-gaming: discount supersedes-chains (a self-split earns its delta once); keep coordinator `useful` ratings as the finder signal. Record the data now; defer the router's solver dimension until ~10 verified proposals exist.

